 "standard_text": "Use square root and cube root symbols to represent solutions to equations of the form x² = p and x³ = p, where p is a positive rational number. Evaluate square roots of small perfect squares and cube roots of small perfect cubes. Know that √2 is irrational.",
 "meta_desc": "Free Grade 8 square roots and cube roots worksheets: perfect squares and cubes, roots of fractions, solve x² = p and x³ = p, estimate roots between whole numbers, and area and volume problems. 100 questions with an answer key.",
 "key_big": "√49 = 7 because 7 × 7 = 49. ∛64 = 4 because 4 × 4 × 4 = 64.",
 "key_sub": "x² = 49 has two solutions (7 and −7). x³ = 64 has one (4).",
 "body_html": "<h2>Square roots and cube roots</h2><p>The <b>square root</b> of a number is the number that, multiplied by itself, gives it: √49 = 7 because 7 × 7 = 49. The <b>cube root</b> uses three equal factors: ∛64 = 4 because 4 × 4 × 4 = 64.</p><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>n</th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th><th>5</th><th>6</th><th>7</th><th>8</th><th>9</th><th>10</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>n²</td><td>1</td><td>4</td><td>9</td><td>16</td><td>25</td><td>36</td><td>49</td><td>64</td><td>81</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>n³</td><td>1</td><td>8</td><td>27</td><td>64</td><td>125</td><td>216</td><td>343</td><td>512</td><td>729</td><td>1,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Solving x² = p and x³ = p</h2><p>x² = 49 has two solutions: x = 7 or x = −7. x³ = −8 has one solution: x = −2.</p><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Between which two whole numbers is √50?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>7² = 49 and 8² = 64.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>50 is between 49 and 64.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 7 and 8 (close to 7)</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Dividing by 2: √36 is 6, not 18.</li><li>Dividing by 3: ∛27 is 3, not 9.</li><li>Forgetting the negative answer of x² = p.</li><li>Thinking a cube root of a negative number does not exist: ∛(−8) = −2.</li></ul>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What is the difference between a square root and a cube root?",
   "a": "A square root uses two equal factors (√25 = 5 because 5 × 5 = 25). A cube root uses three (∛125 = 5 because 5 × 5 × 5 = 125)."
  },
  {
   "q": "Why does x² = 25 have two answers?",
   "a": "Both 5 and −5 square to 25, so x = 5 or x = −5."
  },
  {
   "q": "Can you take the cube root of a negative number?",
   "a": "Yes. ∛(−27) = −3 because (−3) × (−3) × (−3) = −27."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do you estimate a square root?",
   "a": "Find the two perfect squares around the number. √50 is between √49 = 7 and √64 = 8, close to 7."
  }
